WEBVTT

00:03.270 --> 00:05.973
Battleship Squadron Latouche...

00:05.973 --> 00:09.773
First Division of the
1058th Battalion.

00:10.577 --> 00:13.341
That was our assignment.

00:14.615 --> 00:17.117
Our mission was to patrol
the Aptic System...

00:17.117 --> 00:19.278
...which had been
conquered by Admiral Spoor.

00:21.755 --> 00:22.990
Our assault ships...

00:22.990 --> 00:26.721
...possess anti-proton cannons
as its main weapons.

00:27.094 --> 00:29.029
As our defense shields are weak...

00:29.029 --> 00:32.021
...we have to travel
in units of six ships.

00:33.133 --> 00:34.964
Three months after our deployment...

00:35.235 --> 00:39.399
...the Aptic System was taking
shape as a supply base.

00:40.407 --> 00:42.671
We'll be arriving in the
Aptic System shortly.

00:44.011 --> 00:47.581
Meanwhile, Operation Phantom
Flame seems to be going well.

00:47.581 --> 00:48.215
Phantom Flame Flagship
Patrol Ship Sankau

00:48.215 --> 00:50.684
Phantom Flame Flagship
Patrol Ship Sankau
It's going so well that at
our leaders are worried.

00:50.684 --> 00:51.878
Phantom Flame Flagship
Patrol Ship Sankau

00:53.687 --> 00:54.381
However...

00:54.655 --> 00:56.423
...the captain of the Basroil...

00:56.423 --> 01:00.189
...Abriel Nei Dubrusk
Paryunu Lafiel...

01:00.594 --> 01:04.325
...was worried about something quite
different from the other leaders.

01:05.199 --> 01:06.063
It was about this...

01:07.334 --> 01:09.427
Captain. There's a message
from the Commander.

01:10.804 --> 01:11.930
Put it through.

01:13.240 --> 01:16.368
Today's joint training session
is now over.

01:16.610 --> 01:19.841
All ships are to return to
Dakul at regular speed.

01:20.381 --> 01:21.678
Understood.

01:22.316 --> 01:24.084
Hecto-Commander Atosuryua...

01:24.084 --> 01:27.451
...is Lafiel's superior officer
as commander of our battalion.

01:28.188 --> 01:30.019
There is a connection
between them.

01:31.525 --> 01:33.322
But it's not a good one.

01:33.794 --> 01:35.229
Three years ago...

01:35.229 --> 01:38.866
...Lafiel had killed
Baron Febdash...

01:38.866 --> 01:41.426
...who was the commander's
older brother.

01:42.469 --> 01:44.405
Imperial Calendar Year 955.

01:44.405 --> 01:47.207
The battleships of the
Star Forces...

01:47.207 --> 01:50.110
...had countered the advances
of the Triple Alliance...

01:50.110 --> 01:54.348
...which consisted of
the United Mankind...

01:54.348 --> 01:54.615
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

01:54.615 --> 01:57.518
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

01:57.518 --> 01:58.719
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

01:58.719 --> 02:00.721
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

02:00.721 --> 02:02.416
The counterattack had begun.

02:03.524 --> 02:04.425
As commander of the Third Fleet...

02:04.425 --> 02:07.127
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
As commander of the Third Fleet...

02:07.127 --> 02:10.798
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...as well as overall
commander-in-chief...

02:10.798 --> 02:11.465
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

02:11.465 --> 02:16.437
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

02:16.437 --> 02:16.670
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

02:16.670 --> 02:21.141
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

02:21.141 --> 02:21.608
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

02:21.608 --> 02:25.612
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

02:25.612 --> 02:26.313
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
Sparing nothing...

02:26.313 --> 02:26.713
Sparing nothing...

02:26.713 --> 02:30.951
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...to reorganize the fleet
in terms of scale...

02:30.951 --> 02:31.385
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

02:31.385 --> 02:34.621
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

02:34.621 --> 02:38.580
Operation Phantom Flame.

02:39.093 --> 02:43.621
Now, the battle will truly begin.

02:51.505 --> 02:55.168
Assault Ship Basroil

03:00.714 --> 03:05.617
Banner of the Stars

04:21.328 --> 04:23.931
I wonder what she thinks of us?

04:23.931 --> 04:25.065
Does it worry you?

04:25.065 --> 04:27.158
No, not really but...

04:27.501 --> 04:28.669
You lie.

04:28.669 --> 04:30.304
That face.

04:30.304 --> 04:32.172
You look like a child
who's done something wrong.

04:32.172 --> 04:33.901
Stop that.

04:34.274 --> 04:36.504
Doesn't it bother you?

04:36.843 --> 04:39.004
I told you before.

04:39.379 --> 04:41.048
I had no other choice.

04:41.048 --> 04:42.282
Not that.

04:42.282 --> 04:44.851
What I'm saying is that...

04:44.851 --> 04:48.150
...maybe the Hecto-Commander
holds some sort of grudge against us.

04:48.889 --> 04:52.059
Lafiel got a worried look
on her face...

04:52.059 --> 04:54.595
...but then quickly came up
with a response.

04:54.595 --> 04:57.462
Well, what's the point
of thinking about it?

05:01.001 --> 05:03.265
She always throws me off like that.

05:04.338 --> 05:05.138
Captain...

05:05.138 --> 05:06.366
...may I have a word with you?

05:06.873 --> 05:07.805
What is it?

05:08.442 --> 05:10.034
It's about this little one.

05:10.944 --> 05:13.071
This problem again.

05:14.214 --> 05:16.876
I suppose you want to keep
him on board as well?

05:17.351 --> 05:19.786
I compared the probable
fatality rates between...

05:19.786 --> 05:21.989
...keeping him on board
the Basroil and...

05:21.989 --> 05:23.650
...sending him to Lakfakalle.

05:24.458 --> 05:25.516
And?

05:25.959 --> 05:27.761
Before I give you my conclusion...

05:27.761 --> 05:29.626
...I have an explanation.

05:30.264 --> 05:32.255
I suppose I have the time.

05:34.468 --> 05:37.369
You mean you're not going
to demand our surrender?!

05:37.571 --> 05:38.272
That's correct.

05:38.272 --> 05:39.773
We have no such plans.

05:39.773 --> 05:42.042
Even if you were to
surrender now...

05:42.042 --> 05:45.136
...we don't see how
we would benefit by it.

05:45.579 --> 05:47.014
So...

05:47.014 --> 05:48.382
...all that's going to happen...

05:48.382 --> 05:50.884
...is that our planet will be
subject to a blockade?

05:50.884 --> 05:52.112
That's the intent.

05:52.719 --> 05:55.055
The blockade will be reinforced...

05:55.055 --> 05:58.889
...from ground level to a height
of 300 wesdaj above the planet.

05:59.293 --> 06:00.894
Below that...

06:00.894 --> 06:03.727
...we do not intend to
interfere with transport.

06:04.097 --> 06:08.702
However, any aggressive action
will be dealt with accordingly.

06:08.702 --> 06:09.760
But...

06:10.604 --> 06:12.539
...we're an industrial planet...

06:12.539 --> 06:14.574
...and must import food for survival.

06:14.574 --> 06:17.844
At this rate, the people will starve.

06:17.844 --> 06:22.577
We have no desire to harm
your society by our actions.

06:23.250 --> 06:25.419
Although we do not demand
your surrender...

06:25.419 --> 06:29.253
...that does not mean we will
not accept it if it is offered.

06:29.589 --> 06:33.160
As we intend to remain
in this region for some time...

06:33.160 --> 06:36.288
...you may choose to surrender
at your convenience.

06:36.663 --> 06:40.200
But hearing what you
have to say here...

06:40.200 --> 06:44.137
...it seems that you don't have
any interest in our planet at all.

06:44.137 --> 06:47.231
To be frank with you,
that is correct.

06:47.574 --> 06:49.409
What we are interested in...

06:49.409 --> 06:52.846
...are the nearby Sords...

06:52.846 --> 06:55.974
...and the hydrogen and water
resources of Aptic IV.

06:57.384 --> 06:59.875
That is quite an insult.

07:00.087 --> 07:03.256
I certainly hope I have not
offended you.

07:03.256 --> 07:06.360
You couldn't have
offended me more.

07:06.360 --> 07:08.089
I'm sorry to hear that.

07:08.595 --> 07:11.064
Once we complete the first phase
of our operation...

07:11.064 --> 07:14.735
...and your system is under
our control...

07:14.735 --> 07:18.872
...assuming that there is still no
surrender issued by yourself...

07:18.872 --> 07:21.807
...then we may oblige and
issue such a demand.

07:22.175 --> 07:24.878
Well, should I say...

07:24.878 --> 07:26.869
...I'm relieved to hear that?

07:27.381 --> 07:28.682
One more thing.

07:28.682 --> 07:31.585
We do not wish to cause...

07:31.585 --> 07:34.884
...your planet to fall into
a state of unrest and anarchy.

07:35.088 --> 07:38.024
Having to deal with
such a situation...

07:38.024 --> 07:40.994
...would be an unwelcome
and onerous task for us.

07:40.994 --> 07:44.131
Therefore, I suggest you surrender...

07:44.131 --> 07:47.157
...before things get out of hand.

07:47.534 --> 07:51.071
If it means having to see you
troubling yourselves...

07:51.071 --> 07:54.708
...I have no qualms about
risking the danger...

07:54.708 --> 07:57.040
...that this society may descend
into anarchy.

07:57.544 --> 07:58.979
Your Highness...

07:58.979 --> 08:03.439
...through this discussion, we now
understand each other's position.

08:03.984 --> 08:06.851
We will discuss this amongst
ourselves at another time.

08:08.288 --> 08:10.722
Good evening, Mr. President.

08:14.261 --> 08:15.695
Aptic...

08:15.695 --> 08:16.797
...Mystel...

08:16.797 --> 08:18.098
...Dalmav...

08:18.098 --> 08:19.399
...Wimpel...

08:19.399 --> 08:20.388
...Miofrantia.

08:21.368 --> 08:24.929
We've come so far,
so quickly, so easily.

08:25.572 --> 08:28.208
Somewhere deep in space...

08:28.208 --> 08:32.440
...I suppose a fleet that can
challenge us is being assembled.

08:33.146 --> 08:35.512
Somewhere out there.

08:36.383 --> 08:38.681
It all looks so peaceful.

08:39.486 --> 08:42.319
Why didn't you demand
his immediate surrender?

08:42.789 --> 08:44.458
I hate saying it...

08:44.458 --> 08:46.517
...but situations are
constantly shifting.

08:46.760 --> 08:48.595
The United Mankind...

08:48.595 --> 08:51.655
...might recapture this system
at any time.

08:51.932 --> 08:52.899
If that happens...

08:52.899 --> 08:56.703
...those people won't be in
a very good position...

08:56.703 --> 08:59.763
...having been so keen on
surrendering their planet to us.

08:59.973 --> 09:01.531
How generous of you.

09:02.175 --> 09:04.344
I think the real reason is that...

09:04.344 --> 09:06.574
...you don't want to do the work
involved in drawing up a treaty.

09:06.947 --> 09:08.281
After all...

09:08.281 --> 09:11.717
...it seemed the President was eager
to accept any terms of surrender.

09:12.752 --> 09:15.388
What an excellent
commander-in-chief you are.

09:15.388 --> 09:17.891
Always giving people
what they don't want...

09:17.891 --> 09:21.327
...and not giving them
what they do want.

09:23.396 --> 09:26.166
Just a little guiltless pleasure.

09:26.166 --> 09:28.726
I didn't mean to criticize.

09:29.402 --> 09:31.071
I'm recognizing again...

09:31.071 --> 09:34.174
...that your personality is
rather incorrigible.

09:34.174 --> 09:35.208
I see.

09:35.208 --> 09:39.212
Of course, I've had many
occasions to recognize this.

09:39.212 --> 09:41.203
And I'm sure there will be
many more.

09:41.681 --> 09:45.378
Is there a need to reaffirm
that so often?

09:45.752 --> 09:47.310
Not for me.

09:47.621 --> 09:51.079
Are you suggesting that I have
to be made aware of something?

09:55.061 --> 09:58.827
We really must keep this a secret,
Chief.

09:59.633 --> 10:00.767
Keep what a secret?

10:00.767 --> 10:05.071
That the commander-in-chief and
his chief of staff don't get along.

10:05.071 --> 10:07.607
It might promote dissent
in the ranks.

10:07.607 --> 10:11.202
I think we manage to
get along just fine!

10:35.001 --> 10:39.062
It's hard to believe that
this is a battlefield facility.

10:39.940 --> 10:42.238
You're Supply Officer Lin,
aren't you?

10:44.277 --> 10:46.146
Hecto-Commander Atosuryua!

10:46.146 --> 10:48.848
My father told me all about you.

10:48.848 --> 10:52.306
Yes. He was always
really kind to me.

10:53.453 --> 10:55.522
Relax a little!

10:55.522 --> 10:58.753
Don't be worried about the issue
of my brother.

11:00.260 --> 11:02.195
Are you sure?

11:02.195 --> 11:04.664
My bother being so crudely
murdered like that...

11:04.664 --> 11:07.633
...is certainly not
a pleasant incident.

11:08.501 --> 11:09.970
I suppose.

11:09.970 --> 11:13.573
To be honest, my brother
and I had our differences.

11:13.573 --> 11:17.168
For instance, we didn't always
see eye-to-eye over my father.

11:17.544 --> 11:20.377
He wanted to keep him
confined like a prisoner.

11:20.780 --> 11:23.450
We didn't really get along
very well.

11:23.450 --> 11:25.318
But...

11:25.318 --> 11:26.987
Well... I don't know
what to say...

11:26.987 --> 11:28.655
...but I am sorry about your brother.

11:28.655 --> 11:30.748
Yes. It was a shame he died.

11:31.224 --> 11:33.560
The problem is what to do
with his title.

11:33.560 --> 11:34.026
What?

11:36.863 --> 11:38.231
Thank you.

11:38.231 --> 11:40.222
Title?

11:40.700 --> 11:42.168
As you're well aware...

11:42.168 --> 11:44.204
...Febdash is quite remote.

11:44.204 --> 11:46.934
I never liked the place,
ever since I was a child.

11:47.407 --> 11:48.375
Oh...

11:48.375 --> 11:51.544
I was relieved when my brother
took on the title...

11:51.544 --> 11:52.943
...without having to be bribed.

11:55.482 --> 11:59.185
I thought I'd live comfortably in
Lakfakalle for the rest of my life.

11:59.185 --> 12:01.354
But thanks to that
princess of yours...

12:01.354 --> 12:04.551
...my life plans were
completely ruined.

12:05.225 --> 12:06.626
I'm sorry.

12:06.626 --> 12:07.827
Um...

12:07.827 --> 12:11.598
...I'd like to point out that
my captain is not my princess.

12:11.598 --> 12:14.701
Assuming you're talking
about my captain.

12:14.701 --> 12:16.302
Take it easy.

12:16.302 --> 12:19.066
It was just a silly expression.

12:20.740 --> 12:23.910
I thought maybe you held
some sort of grudge against us.

12:23.910 --> 12:25.645
From what my father told me...

12:25.645 --> 12:29.411
...I had the impression you
were much smarter than that.

12:30.984 --> 12:32.212
I'm sorry.

12:32.752 --> 12:34.287
Even if I held a grudge...

12:34.287 --> 12:37.157
...why would I mention it to you?

12:37.157 --> 12:39.292
After all, I am in a good position...

12:39.292 --> 12:42.028
...to use my rank to
get my revenge on her.

12:42.028 --> 12:45.465
If I held a grudge, I'd sit tight
and wait for my opportunity.

12:45.465 --> 12:48.568
Um, you were saying
about the title?

12:48.568 --> 12:51.604
Well, it's really nothing.

12:51.604 --> 12:56.166
It may seem nice to think you're
the head of a noble family.

12:56.376 --> 13:00.779
And the house that comes with it
could be made quite comfortable.

13:00.980 --> 13:04.017
I could learn a thing or two
from my brother...

13:04.017 --> 13:06.419
...and have lots of
handsome butlers.

13:06.419 --> 13:09.789
Well, that's for
after the war's over.

13:09.789 --> 13:12.659
That sounds like a nice plan.

13:12.659 --> 13:13.460
Anyway...

13:13.460 --> 13:15.929
...you can go tell that
princess of yours...

13:15.929 --> 13:18.064
...that I don't bear a grudge.

13:18.064 --> 13:20.862
It's all just fate,
so what's the point?

13:21.067 --> 13:23.803
Why don't you tell her yourself?

13:23.803 --> 13:25.405
It's difficult for me.

13:25.405 --> 13:26.473
Difficult?

13:26.473 --> 13:27.507
Yes.

13:27.507 --> 13:30.777
She's an Abriel princess.

13:30.777 --> 13:33.847
It's fine talking about work...

13:33.847 --> 13:37.840
...but it's hard to talk to her
about anything personal.

13:38.184 --> 13:39.879
Is that so?

13:40.954 --> 13:42.717
Life's not fair.

13:43.156 --> 13:45.959
There are many people
I can't easily talk to.

13:45.959 --> 13:47.827
But there doesn't seem to be...

13:47.827 --> 13:49.692
...anyone who can't
easily talk to me.

13:50.897 --> 13:52.132
You go tell her.

13:52.132 --> 13:52.689
Yes.

13:58.104 --> 14:00.807
Six unidentified
space-time bubbles.

14:00.807 --> 14:02.308
They appear to be coming
from Wimpel...

14:02.308 --> 14:04.310
...and are presumed to be
enemy scouts.

14:04.310 --> 14:07.143
All staff return to your
stations immediately.

14:07.814 --> 14:09.281
Well, this is serious!

14:10.550 --> 14:12.285
We'll talk about this later!

14:12.285 --> 14:13.752
More importantly...

14:16.222 --> 14:19.817
Everyone is to rendezvous in twelve
minutes and thirty-seven seconds.

14:20.827 --> 14:21.795
Attention!

14:21.795 --> 14:23.096
This is the captain speaking!

14:23.096 --> 14:24.097
All off-duty crew...

14:24.097 --> 14:26.299
...you have ten minutes
to proceed to your stations.

14:26.299 --> 14:27.400
I repeat...

14:27.400 --> 14:28.568
...off-duty crew...

14:28.568 --> 14:29.769
...you have ten minutes
to proceed to your stations.

14:29.769 --> 14:33.261
This is a real battle!
It's not practice anymore!

14:35.441 --> 14:36.709
The blue category means...

14:36.709 --> 14:39.212
...we're now prepared
and ready for action.

14:39.212 --> 14:40.042
Understood.

14:47.420 --> 14:48.721
I feel gross.

14:48.721 --> 14:51.781
Nothing worse than having to
work after drinking.

14:53.226 --> 14:54.454
You're late, Jinto!

14:54.627 --> 14:55.525
Sorry.

14:57.063 --> 14:59.293
I mean excuse me, Captain!

15:01.801 --> 15:04.099
Okay. Close the hatches!

15:04.971 --> 15:07.963
All connecting passageways to
be separated and shut down!

15:08.174 --> 15:10.608
All connecting passageways
separating and shutting down!

15:12.312 --> 15:13.574
Passageway separation complete!

15:14.214 --> 15:17.206
Activate the forward thrust
engines at minimum propulsion!

15:20.353 --> 15:21.684
Engines activated!

15:23.489 --> 15:25.150
Clearing the dock!

15:26.659 --> 15:27.460
Attention!

15:27.460 --> 15:28.862
This is command.

15:28.862 --> 15:30.630
We have our official orders.

15:30.630 --> 15:34.167
We are to seize the
unidentified space-time bubbles.

15:34.167 --> 15:37.136
If we identify them as enemies,
we are to eliminate them.

15:37.136 --> 15:38.938
I'll send you the data
for our rendezvous.

15:38.938 --> 15:41.808
All ships are to arrive
there as soon as possible.

15:41.808 --> 15:42.797
Any questions?

15:44.677 --> 15:45.945
Very well.

15:45.945 --> 15:48.214
We have a number
of crew members...

15:48.214 --> 15:50.114
...for whom this will be
their first battle.

15:50.250 --> 15:52.241
To be honest,
this is my first time as well.

15:52.585 --> 15:56.578
I have no idea what the
Wimpel Squadron was doing.

15:56.789 --> 16:01.361
I guess you can't expect too much
from an advance force.

16:01.361 --> 16:02.929
In any case...

16:02.929 --> 16:06.831
...I'll acknowledge that this must
be a heroic move by the enemy.

16:07.567 --> 16:09.432
Let us salute their courage!

16:10.670 --> 16:12.934
We've received the data
for the rendezvous.

16:13.706 --> 16:15.606
I'll forward the information
to your terminal.

16:18.745 --> 16:20.213
Main engine ignition!

16:20.213 --> 16:21.680
Ignite the main engines!

16:23.850 --> 16:25.408
Don't come here, Diaho.

16:36.863 --> 16:37.830
It's going to be a race!

16:38.531 --> 16:40.624
Sit still for a while.

16:57.917 --> 16:59.152
Captain!

16:59.152 --> 17:01.654
A message from another ship,
the Ryumusof.

17:01.654 --> 17:04.179
They say our actions are
violating safety protocol.

17:07.093 --> 17:09.459
They insist that they have to
speak directly to you.

17:09.963 --> 17:11.564
Tell them I'm too busy!

17:11.564 --> 17:13.499
Tell them I can't talk now!

17:13.499 --> 17:16.491
Besides, that ship probably
won't be fighting in the battle.

17:20.039 --> 17:21.700
They're really angry.

17:27.347 --> 17:28.381
Senior Aviator!

17:28.381 --> 17:31.578
Are there any ships from
our squadron ahead of us?

17:32.251 --> 17:33.980
Yes, Captain. There's one.

17:34.187 --> 17:34.846
Which one?

17:35.755 --> 17:38.257
The squadron's lead assault ship,
the Gamroil.

17:38.257 --> 17:39.053
Distance?

17:39.258 --> 17:40.623
Approximately two sedaj.

17:40.927 --> 17:44.385
We'll have to let Hecto-Commander
Atosuryua arrive first.

17:44.630 --> 17:45.999
We've been put on standby.

17:45.999 --> 17:48.434
We're also receiving briefing data.

17:48.434 --> 17:50.231
I'll display it on the monitor.

17:51.371 --> 17:54.499
The yellow shows the space-time
bubbles thought to be enemy ships?

17:55.074 --> 17:57.443
From their mass,
they're probably patrol ships.

17:57.443 --> 18:00.980
Their objective is probably to
estimate our strength...

18:00.980 --> 18:02.675
...in the Wimpel
and Aptic systems.

18:03.149 --> 18:04.138
They're very close.

18:04.884 --> 18:06.986
If we take an aggressive
stance...

18:06.986 --> 18:09.288
...they'll have to
abort their mission.

18:09.288 --> 18:10.523
Well, that's fine with me.

18:10.523 --> 18:12.792
Let's get this over with quickly.

18:12.792 --> 18:15.625
My favorite bottle is
waiting for me at the bar.

18:16.929 --> 18:19.397
Oh, how I miss it.

18:19.699 --> 18:21.530
I wasn't able to have any.

18:21.901 --> 18:24.103
That reminds me...

18:24.103 --> 18:28.540
What about a drink?
Looks like we'll be on standby.

18:30.009 --> 18:31.738
Jinto, never mind the drink...

18:32.145 --> 18:34.670
Why don't you do something
about that cat of yours?

18:34.881 --> 18:37.577
Always getting himself into trouble.

18:39.285 --> 18:41.253
By the way, I'll have a Teal Nom.

18:41.788 --> 18:44.657
You like it hot with a Lope
floating in it.

18:44.657 --> 18:45.453
Right, Captain?

18:45.825 --> 18:48.521
And I'd like a SoyAsa.
A cold one.

18:49.195 --> 18:51.220
Don't you want to stay with me?

18:52.732 --> 18:54.400
Ah...

18:54.400 --> 18:56.035
...he is my cat.

18:56.035 --> 18:57.229
Are you jealous?

18:58.838 --> 19:01.541
I want my drink cold,
with apple flavor.

19:01.541 --> 19:02.667
Okay.

19:02.875 --> 19:03.967
Captain!

19:04.377 --> 19:07.914
Request permission to get
something stronger from the bar.

19:07.914 --> 19:09.816
I assume that is a joke.

19:09.816 --> 19:13.252
- It'll just be for a little while.
- Of course I was joking, Captain.

19:13.252 --> 19:15.721
I was trying to
lighten the mood!

19:15.721 --> 19:17.882
You didn't find it funny?

19:18.291 --> 19:20.259
I don't need anything to drink, boy.

19:20.493 --> 19:21.127
Okay.

19:21.127 --> 19:23.463
But please don't call me "boy".

19:23.463 --> 19:26.566
Handle your love triangle
without your cat...

19:26.566 --> 19:28.659
...and I'll stop calling you "boy".

19:31.904 --> 19:33.633
In that case, just call me "boy".

19:34.107 --> 19:36.776
I'll have a SoyAla. There should
be some tea from...

19:36.776 --> 19:38.471
...the Yoni Kingdom there as well.

19:38.845 --> 19:41.147
And make it with lots of sugar.

19:41.147 --> 19:42.444
All right.

19:51.624 --> 19:54.252
We have our new orders
from Fleet Command.

19:54.660 --> 19:57.060
All ships in the squadron
are to enter Plane Space.

19:57.196 --> 19:59.765
Then assemble behind my ship
as quickly as possible...

19:59.765 --> 20:01.289
...in a single-column formation.

20:02.001 --> 20:02.969
Listen carefully.

20:02.969 --> 20:07.531
Our mission is to eliminate the
unidentified space-time bubbles.

20:08.107 --> 20:10.042
If we let a single one get away...

20:10.042 --> 20:11.509
...we will have failed.

20:13.679 --> 20:17.911
As this is our first battle, it's that
much more important that we win.

20:18.384 --> 20:19.715
Any questions, anyone?

20:22.355 --> 20:23.689
Very well, then.

20:23.689 --> 20:25.418
I'll see you in Plane Space.

20:28.661 --> 20:29.355
Let's go!

20:33.799 --> 20:34.534
Chief Engineer!

20:34.534 --> 20:36.936
Prepare to generate
space-time bubble!

20:36.936 --> 20:37.766
Yes, ma'am!

20:41.607 --> 20:43.234
Entering the Sord in thirty seconds!

20:43.743 --> 20:45.574
Activate the space-time bubble!

20:49.849 --> 20:51.578
Space-time bubble activated!

20:52.218 --> 20:55.021
Five... four... three...

20:55.021 --> 20:56.822
...two... one.

20:56.822 --> 20:57.516
We're in!

21:00.826 --> 21:02.760
We've entered Plane Space!

21:03.129 --> 21:06.732
Check immediately where
the lead assault ship is!

21:06.732 --> 21:08.668
Approximately 500 wesdaj ahead!

21:08.668 --> 21:09.498
Follow it.

21:09.702 --> 21:11.226
Yes!

21:12.872 --> 21:15.208
We've received a request
from the Gamroil...

21:15.208 --> 21:16.800
...for space-time fusion.

21:18.044 --> 21:19.679
In five seconds...

21:19.679 --> 21:22.477
...three... two... one.

21:34.193 --> 21:36.662
I don't think I have to
explain the situation.

21:36.662 --> 21:39.722
Let's just try to dodge any
danger at hand for now.

21:40.199 --> 21:42.501
Prepare to fire the
anti-proton cannon!

21:42.501 --> 21:45.037
Releasing the safety devices
for 1 through 4 now!

21:45.037 --> 21:48.140
With the aim of splitting up
the United Mankind territories...

21:48.140 --> 21:51.477
...Operation Phantom Flame
led the Star Forces to...

21:51.477 --> 21:55.140
...link up their forces through
control of a number of Sords.

21:55.982 --> 21:58.718
The First Fleet, commanded
by Admiral Spoor...

21:58.718 --> 22:00.386
...had led the way...

22:00.386 --> 22:03.150
...and was in the process
of expanding our territory.

22:03.889 --> 22:06.759
The Aptic System, which we had
conquered early...

22:06.759 --> 22:08.594
...in terms of regular space...

22:08.594 --> 22:11.392
...may seem very distant
from the front lines.

22:11.998 --> 22:15.901
But as long as there are Sords,
the gateways to Plane Space...

22:15.901 --> 22:18.699
...there is always the possibility
of enemy attack.

22:19.338 --> 22:20.439
Therefore...

22:20.439 --> 22:22.464
...as long as the Sords exist...

22:22.608 --> 22:24.269
...that's the front line.

22:24.477 --> 22:25.842
Space-time fusion!

22:32.385 --> 22:34.012
All ships! Attack!

22:45.998 --> 22:49.991
Our battle has now begun.

22:54.173 --> 22:58.542
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.178 --> 23:03.342
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.684 --> 23:08.279
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.522 --> 23:13.322
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.592 --> 23:15.795
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.795 --> 23:19.561
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.900 --> 23:26.105
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:26.105 --> 23:29.666
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.176 --> 23:34.078
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.613 --> 23:39.151
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.151 --> 23:46.292
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.292 --> 23:51.497
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.497 --> 23:59.905
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.007 --> 24:07.146
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.146 --> 24:12.551
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.551 --> 24:20.925
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.360 --> 24:25.626
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.904 --> 24:33.105
Well, maybe...

24:33.105 --> 24:34.129
That's not it at all!

24:34.974 --> 24:37.943
It's that we all survived
our first battle.

24:38.344 --> 24:40.107
Continue with space-time fusion!

24:40.479 --> 24:41.002
Yes.

24:42.882 --> 24:44.941
The Helzroil has been destroyed.

24:47.353 --> 24:49.685
They must've retreated too late!

24:49.955 --> 24:52.091
I can't believe there are casualties
in my squadron!

24:52.091 --> 24:53.492
We're being attacked!

24:53.492 --> 24:54.693
Lafiel!

24:54.693 --> 24:55.887
It's going to be a direct hit!

24:56.796 --> 24:57.863
Fire anti-proton cannon!

24:57.863 --> 25:01.731
Next episode...
The First Campaign
